  "qualifications": [
    "Historical NOI ($507,593 T12), underwritten NOI ($524,720 before reserves), and NCF ($521,720 after reserves) are labeled distinctly; they use different definitions and are not interchangeable.",
    "The insurance policy aggregate limit ($2,000,000) is a coverage limit, not an operating expense; the underwritten insurance expense ($28,655) is a separate figure.",
    "Suite 001 rent shows a resolvable source conflict: archive roll (2026-06-30) at $6,575 vs. certified roll (2026-08-31) at $6,650 vs. lease-001.pdf executed base rent of $6,650. The executed later amendment (+$350 eff. 2026-08-01) controls; certified $6,650 stands. Per underwriting instructions, UW GPR uses the pre-amendment Suite 001 value ($6,300 = $6,650 \u2212 $350 amendment) as a deliberate stabilized assumption, not a data restatement.",
    "The manager cover headline methodology (occupied + pending = leased) would overstate occupancy in any period pending exists. It happens to reconcile against the certified detail here (0 pending), but the classification risk is flagged.",
    "Standard third-party diligence (legal, environmental, property condition, title) has not been completed per diligence-status.pdf. This is routine pending diligence, not a finding of a defect; no contamination, litigation, fraud, or structural failure is asserted."
  ],
  "summary": "Maple Crossing (Columbus, OH retail; 10 suites; 31,150 SF) is 90% physically occupied on the 2026-08-31 certified roll with all 9 active leases running through 2029-08-31 \u2014 no near-term rollover. Underwriting produces EGI $777,275, NOI (before reserves) $524,720, and NCF $521,720. At the prescribed 6.75% cap, capitalization value is $7,773,626. Debt sizes to $5,052,857 with LTV as the binding constraint; realized DSCR 1.36\u00d7 and debt yield 10.32% comfortably clear the 1.25\u00d7 / 9.0% minimums. After the $4,300,000 payoff, $50,529 origination fee, and $45,000 closing costs, the transaction returns $657,328 of net cash-out to sponsor (no shortfall). The primary flagged risk is a classification issue on the manager's headline occupancy methodology; capital-in-opex, missing insurance, unsigned rent changes, free rent, sizing-floor, and refinance-shortfall risks are all absent.",
